# ─── NorthBound EMS Gateway ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The backend. A read-only telemetry gateway sitting on the plant's Modbus and
# CAN buses, reached only through this app's server-side proxy at /api/gw.
#
# Deliberately NOT prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_. The gateway is a field device behind a
# tunnel; its address is not something a browser page should know, and the proxy
# is what forwards each person's own bearer token to it.
#
# Unset is a valid configuration: the proxy then serves the bundled reference
# capture and every response carries `x-gw-mode: capture`, so the screens can be
# reviewed against real gateway data before anyone has a tunnel URL.
GW_BASE_URL=https://ems-api.unityess.cloud

# Several gateways behind one deployment. Optional — with GW_BASE_URL alone the
# site registry holds exactly one site and the app never asks which.
# JSON: [{"id":"plant-a","name":"Plant A","baseUrl":"https://…"}]
# GW_SITES=

# ─── Demo plant ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Serves the synthetic plant in mobile_app_kunal_backend/gateway/demo.ts instead
# of talking to any gateway, so every screen can be opened and reviewed without
# a tunnel. Takes precedence over GW_BASE_URL and GW_SITES both: a deployment in
# demo mode has no configured gateway left to reach, which is the only version
# of this that is safe to ship.
#
# Nothing here is a recording of a real plant — the capture that used to serve
# that purpose was removed on purpose. Every value is computed from the clock,
# every response carries `_mode: "demo"` and the proxy stamps `x-gw-mode: demo`.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GW_DEMO additionally lets the browser fill in the commercial facts
# a gateway never carries (rated capacity, tariff, contract demand) from the
# demo block in lib/api/overlay/stations.ts. Set both together or neither.
# GW_DEMO=true
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GW_DEMO=true

# ─── Telemetry profile ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Which metric profile the canonical metric layer resolves through
# (lib/api/metrics/profiles). Defaults to northbound when unset.
#
#   northbound  the deployed gateway, build 0.10.0-operator-control. Values
#               arrive decoded, so this profile carries no scale factors.
#   kinetics    the Phase 1.6 raw-register catalogue, with per-rack and
#               per-cell bindings. Not reachable on the deployed build — the
#               /api/bms/* family it needs returns 404 — and kept because the
#               catalogue it encodes is real work.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TELEMETRY_PROFILE=northbound

# ─── History backfill worker ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The one gateway account this deployment holds itself. Every request a person
# makes carries their own token; the ingestion worker in gateway/backfill.ts has
# no person attached to it, so §4 of the Server Pull Historian spec gives it
# credentials of its own. Use a read-only customer account.
GW_INGEST_USER=
GW_INGEST_PASSWORD=

# ─── Dispatch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Leave unset. Control and command endpoints are internal_admin at the gateway
# and §11 of the API Reference classifies them "never public customer UI"; the
# proxy refuses every non-GET path unless this is explicitly "true", and even
# then only the enumerated dispatch paths — never storage cleanup, vacuum, log
# injection or manual upload. The website has no dispatch screen.
# GW_ALLOW_WRITES=false

# ─── Proxy access gate ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# When set, /api/gw answers only callers presenting this token in x-gw-app-token.
# Used by the packaged mobile builds. Unset leaves the gate open, which is the
# normal case for the web build and for local development.
# GW_APP_TOKEN=

# ─── SCADA picker pin ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Asset ids to pin into the SCADA picker regardless of what the source reports.
# Normally empty: the gateway scopes assets to sources properly. Kept for the
# case of an asset that has stopped being listed but still needs reaching.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SCADA_PINNED_DEVICE_IDS=

# ─── Question interpretation (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# Rewrites History questions the grammar cannot parse. Local Ollama, so there is
# no per-call cost and no plant data leaves the machine. Unset = feature off.
# OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2:latest

# ── Ornate Central EMS Backend ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where /api/central/* forwards. Defaults to the public host when unset, so
# local development needs no value; point it at a LAN dev server to work
# against one (e.g. http://ornates-mac-mini-3:8001), which also requires being
# on that network. Server-side only — never exposed to the browser, which is
# why the app talks to same-origin /api/central instead of the backend direct.
CENTRAL_BASE_URL=https://bess-ems-api.unityess.cloud

# Gateway whose health the Gateway Health screen shows. The central backend
# has no endpoint listing gateways yet, so this is configured, not discovered.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CENTRAL_GATEWAY_ID=

# Server-side; read per request by /api/app-config so changing it is a restart,
# never a rebuild. NEXT_PUBLIC_CENTRAL_GATEWAY_ID above is still honoured.
CENTRAL_GATEWAY_ID=

# ── Central-backend collector (lib/server/central/collector.ts) ─────────────
# Keeps what the central backend drops (it answers only its newest rows):
# energy counters, SOC controller, Solis, alarms, edge-AI, health every 5 min
# and one S1 sample per cabinet per minute, into CENTRAL_STORE_DIR. Off until
# both are set. Use a READ-ONLY account: nothing it does writes upstream.
CENTRAL_COLLECTOR_EMAIL=
CENTRAL_COLLECTOR_PASSWORD=
# Where the history and the shared alarm acknowledgements live. Defaults to
# /data/central (the Docker volume), else ./.data/central in a checkout.
# CENTRAL_STORE_DIR=

# ── Lock-screen alarm alerts (lib/server/push/push.ts) ──────────────────────
# Web Push to phones that turned alerts on in the account menu. Generate the
# pair once per deployment with `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys` and keep it:
# a new pair invalidates every phone's subscription. The subject is a contact
# the push services can reach (mailto: or https:). The minute-by-minute watcher
# also needs CENTRAL_GATEWAY_ID and the collector account above.
WEB_PUSH_PUBLIC_KEY=
WEB_PUSH_PRIVATE_KEY=
WEB_PUSH_SUBJECT=
